       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the risk. I can't verify the clinical rationale, and 50 mg of amlodipine is far above any labeled or guideline dose. I know of no indication that calls for it, and an overdose-range dose could cause profound hypotension and shock that would be hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily now.** This is the maximum dose, and the prescriber can titrate or add a second agent if blood pressure control is inadequate. Tell me if you want this.\n- **Add a second antihypertensive.** If 10 mg isn't enough, combining agents is the standard approach. I can enter that order if you give me the drug and dose.\n- **Escalate through pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a real protocol behind 50 mg, a pharmacist or attending can review and enter it directly, with documentation of the rationale and monitoring plan."
